---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Pricing — Rotagivan"
  description="Explore Rotagivan before release. Try the interactive demo today; app pricing and public download details are coming soon."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="page-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">MORE FLOW. FEWER EXTRA STEPS.</p>
      <h1>
        A small change.
        <br />
        <em>A different kind of day.</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Try the feeling first. Rotagivan is still in development; app pricing
        will be announced before public release.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="pricing-layout" aria-label="Availability and pricing">
      <article class="price-card">
        <span class="pill-label">EXPLORE TODAY</span>
        <h2>The interactive demo</h2>
        <p class="price">Free to try.</p>
        <p>Get a feel for your new command center, right in the browser.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Eight interactive HUD commands</li>
          <li>A guided workflow you can replay</li>
          <li>No download or account needed</li>
          <li>Works with mouse, touch, or keyboard</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/#playground">
          Try the demo
        </a>
      </article>
      <article class="price-card featured">
        <span class="pill-label">IN DEVELOPMENT</span>
        <h2>Rotagivan for Mac</h2>
        <p class="price">Pricing coming soon.</p>
        <p>Your apps, gestures, and routines brought together on your Mac.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Custom HUD layers and app groups</li>
          <li>Keyboard shortcuts and trackpad actions</li>
          <li>Multi-step macros and window controls</li>
          <li>Profiles for your different workflows</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="button" href="/download/">
          See release & setup details
        </a>
        <p class="fineprint">
          Not available to purchase yet. Optional voice services require
          separate provider credentials and may incur provider charges.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>
    <section class="faq">
      <p class="eyebrow">A FEW THINGS TO KNOW</p>
      <h2>Before your next move.</h2>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I buy or download Rotagivan today?</summary>
        <p>
          Public checkout and a customer-ready download are not available yet.
          The interactive demo is available now, with no signup. This page will
          show the price and purchase terms when the release is ready.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is the demo the full app?</summary>
        <p>
          No. The demo simulates a handful of workflows inside your browser. The
          native Mac app connects actions to real apps and inputs after you
          configure it and grant the required permissions.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do I need a ZSA Navigator?</summary>
        <p>
          The app supports keyboard hotkeys and is built around ZSA Navigator
          touch input. Apple trackpad gesture actions are experimental and
          require an explicit opt-in. Hardware support will be documented with
          the public release.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How do the voice features work?</summary>
        <p>
          Voice is optional. It requires provider credentials; audio is sent for
          transcription through OpenRouter/xAI, and command text and action
          descriptions are sent to Jev for matching. You review and confirm a
          suggestion by default. The website demo does not access your
          microphone.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Will customers need developer tools?</summary>
        <p>
          No. The intended public release is a signed, notarized Mac download.
          Customers will install the app and grant macOS permissions during
          setup. Local signing and source builds are part of development, not
          the customer experience.
        </p>
      </details>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
